## What each outcome means (root-cause table)

| Finding | Root cause | Fix owner |
|---|---|---|
| Step 1 `notAfter` past / issuer untrusted / SAN wrong | Gateway serving cert expired or misissued | Renew/replace the `credentialName` secret in `int-istio-system` |
| Step 2 secret cert ≠ what's served | Gateway serving stale cert | Roll the gateway deployment to reload |
| Step 3 DestinationRule with `SIMPLE`/`MUTUAL` on istio pod | TLS-mode mismatch gateway→pod | Set DR to `ISTIO_MUTUAL` or delete the override |
| Step 4 log references upstream + verify fail | mTLS trust skew gateway→pod | Restart istiod / check trust bundle |
| Step 5 workload cert expired | istiod not rotating | Restart pod; investigate istiod |

Start at Step 1 — it partitions the entire problem into "client-facing cert" vs "mesh mTLS" with a single command. Paste back the `subject/issuer/dates/SAN` output and the Step 4 gateway log line, and I'll pin the exact root cause and the minimal remediation.

